      "message": "if we are making the keycode maps always mutable, then we should provide getter/setter methods instead of letting anyone directly modify the variable.\n\nIt wasn\u0027t worth putting in the proper API when only 1 or 2 boards needed it to be mutable, but if it will always be mutable, then we should protect against common code from accidentally over-writing a value when it didn\u0027t mean to (when it is accessing keycap_label).\n\nWe had that protection before (common code not accidentally changing the variable) because we still had some boards being compiled with the variable as a const, which would have failed to compile if common code modified the variable.",
